 "_readme": "The people who made Cassini-Huygens happen, for the credits roll after the Grand Finale (finale.html) and the About window (window.cassiniTeam). build.py bakes it in. Every name and role comes from the sources listed at the end, as those pages write them (initials where they give only initials); obvious typos on the source page were fixed (Scott G. Edgington, Norbert Krupp, S. Chatterjee, Hao Cao). Add a name only with a source. Sections: title, sub (optional line), people [{role, name, note}], names [plain list], text, groups [same shape, with their own title]. The order follows Sam's wish: the imaging team first, since every picture in Cassini OS is theirs, then the mission's leaders, then navigation, then everyone else.",
 "intro": {
  "head": "Cassini was made by people.",
  "text": "Thousands of them built it, flew it for twenty years and read what it sent home. These are some of their names, as NASA and ESA list them."
